      "text": [
        " : سَأَلْتُهُ عَنْ رَجُلٍ أَسْكَنَ دَارَهُ رَجُلاً مُدَّةَ حَيَاتِهِ فَقَالَ \"يَجُوزُ لَهُ وَ لَيْسَ لَهُ أَنْ يُخْرِجَهُ\" قُلْتُ فَلَهُ وَ لِعَقِبِهِ قَالَ \"يَجُوزُ لَهُ\" وَ سَأَلْتُهُ عَنْ رَجُلٍ أَسْكَنَ رَجُلاً وَ لَمْ يُوَقِّتْ لَهُ شَيْئاً قَالَ \"يُخْرِجُهُ صَاحِبُ اَلدَّارِ إِذَا شَاءَ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5597 - Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Faddal narrated from Ahmad ibn Umar Al-Halabi from his father from Abu Abdullah (as) who said: I asked Imam (as) about a man who allowed another man to reside in his house for the duration of his life.\nImam (as) replied: \"It is permissible for him, and he does not have the right to evict him.\"\nI asked: \"Does this also apply to his descendants?\"\nImam (as) replied: \"It is permissible for him.\"\nI then asked Imam (as) about a man who allowed another man to reside in his house without specifying any time period.\nImam (as) replied: \"The owner of the house may evict him whenever he wishes.\""
        ]
      }
    },
